ad aquarium (into the fishbowl?) is what I used to think the vault
message actually was. Therefore I suggest that occasionally a secret
teleport cupboard be created with the text "ad aquarium" written
outside it.

Using the teleport trap lands the player in a 2*2 vault-like room
sporting 3 squares of water that contain at least one nasty fishy thing
and one kelp frond. The fourth square should be land and is where the
player stands, obviously. Each of the four sqaures contains a single
gold piece (to make it look a bit like a vault if you use gold
detect/obj detect, and the land square should contain a rusty pickaxe,
to allow you to get back out again.

It would add a little extra challenge and flavour to the game, make the
player a little more wary (or maybe unwary) of vaults, create an
opportunity to obtain a pickaxe without entering the mines, provide a
handy source of water for dipping and also get a little extra mileage
out of the underused ; monster types. Shouldn't break bones or save
compatibility either, if I understand these things correctly (which I
probably don't.)

Anyone want to patch it?



